From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xdgshellwindow: keep the requested geometry of fullscreen and maximized windows
Description:
 When a client acknowledges a configure event and commits before it has
 attached a buffer of the new size, KWin clamps the new window geometry to
 the old buffer. XdgSurfaceWindow::maybeUpdateMoveResizeGeometry() then
 takes this interim frame geometry over as the move resize geometry, since
 no configure event is pending any more. Every configure event sent after
 that without a new moveResize(), for example for a change of the activated
 or suspended state, asks the client for the interim size, and the client
 keeps it although the window is still fullscreen or maximized.
 .
 Seen after rotating the screen of a phone from portrait (415x910) to
 landscape (946x415): a fullscreen video player stayed at 415x415, a
 maximized window at 415x357, i.e. the new size clamped to the old buffer.
 Leaving and entering fullscreen again fixed it at once.
 .
 The size of a fullscreen or fully maximized window is dictated by the
 compositor, so keep the requested geometry for these windows and do not
 take over the committed one. The frame geometry still follows what the
 client commits.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
--- a/src/xdgshellwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/xdgshellwindow.cpp
@@ -194,6 +194,15 @@
         }
     }
 
+    // The geometry of a fullscreen or maximized window is dictated by the compositor. The client
+    // can commit another size for a while, e.g. when it acknowledges a configure event before it
+    // has attached a buffer of the new size (the window geometry is then clamped to the old
+    // buffer). Keep the requested geometry in that case, otherwise every following configure
+    // event, e.g. for an activation change, would ask the client to keep the interim size.
+    if (isRequestedFullScreen() || requestedMaximizeMode() == MaximizeFull) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     setMoveResizeGeometry(rect);
 }
 
